            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a cousin, then the Kannada for a brother."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಬಂಧು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಂಧು — bandhu — \"kin; a relative\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಬ್ಬಕ್ಕೆ ಎಲ್ಲಾ ಬಂಧುಗಳು ನಮ್ಮ ಮನೆಗೆ ಬಂದರು. habbakke ellā bandhugaḷu namma manege bandaru. All our relatives came to our house for the festival."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Plural: ಬಂಧುಗಳು, bandhugaḷu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಂಧು (bandhu)-ಬಳಗ, relatives and friends."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಬಂಧು (bandhu) is borrowed from Sanskrit bandhu, \"kinsman\" (CDIAL 9144), from bandh, \"to bind\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
